-- DJM Player staging application permissions bootstrap
-- STAGING BOOTSTRAP ONLY. Do not run against production.
-- Apply after application schema, functions, triggers and RLS.
--
-- Exact current-production non-owner ACL snapshot for recovered DJM objects:
--   405 functions
--   117 tables
--   2 sequences
--   schema USAGE for private/djm_os
--   1,386 permission statements
--
-- Production ACL body MD5: 2bfcee2c792e537748a3f17cdd2d45e4
--
-- IMPORTANT:
--   - This file is intentionally object-specific.
--   - It does NOT reference or modify staging-only platform_server_* RPCs.
--   - It does NOT alter the public schema ACL itself.
--   - It normalizes default CREATE FUNCTION PUBLIC EXECUTE before restoring
--     the effective production ACL for each recovered function.
--
-- Do not replace this with GRANT ... ON ALL FUNCTIONS/TABLES IN SCHEMA:
-- doing so could unintentionally expose white-label platform objects.

begin;

